course: dictionary
lesson: 10034
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Terminally is one of them. In serious talk, «terminally ill» means someone has an illness that cannot be cured and will lead to death. This is a gentle word, so use it carefully and only when it is really needed.
explain: The other meaning is a joke. Someone might say, «He's terminally lazy», or «That film was terminally boring». Nobody is ill here. Terminally means extremely or hopelessly, so the speaker is saying that laziness or boredom is very strong.
explain: How do you choose? Look at the words around it. Illness, doctors or hospices point to the serious meaning. Lazy, boring or uncool, said with a laugh, points to the joking meaning. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Terminally is an adverb, so it tells you how strong or serious something is.
fact: «Terminally ill» means ill with an illness that cannot be cured.
fact: Hospices are places that care for people who are terminally ill and help them be comfortable.
fact: «Terminally boring» is an informal, joking way to say extremely boring.
fact: When a word has two meanings, read the context to choose the right one.
exercise: «He is terminally ill, and the doctors cannot cure his illness.» What does terminally mean here? | Extremely, in a joking way | Happily | Very quickly | *Having an illness that cannot be cured and will lead to death
exercise: Jo says, «This homework is terminally boring!» What does terminally mean here? | Late | Having an illness that cannot be cured | *Extremely, in a joking way | Quietly
exercise: Which phrase uses the joking sense? | terminally ill | a hospice for people who are terminally ill | *terminally uncool
test: Which sentence uses the serious meaning? | «That game is terminally boring.» | «He's terminally lazy.» | *«The family visited her, as she was terminally ill.»
test: What does a hospice do for people who are terminally ill? | *Helps them be comfortable | Sells cakes and tea | Repairs cars | Teaches them to swim
exam: In «The teacher said the meeting was terminally dull», what does terminally mean? | *Extremely, in a joking way | Very early | Slowly and quietly | Having an illness that cannot be cured
